Define TTerminal::LogEvent out of line, as the files calling it need.

TTerminal::LogEvent is defined `inline` in Terminal.cpp, but the file
systems (FtpFileSystem.cpp and others) call it too. An inline function must
be defined in every translation unit that uses it; when it is not, the
program is ill-formed, and whether it links depends on the compiler keeping
an out-of-line copy. An optimizing clang build (-O2, -O3) inlines every
call within Terminal.cpp and emits none, so the other files' calls are
undefined at link time. Without `inline` the definition is the one every
caller links to; the calls within Terminal.cpp may still be inlined.
Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/Terminal.cpp
+++ b/source/core/Terminal.cpp
@@ -3473,1 +3473,1 @@
-void __fastcall inline TTerminal::LogEvent(const UnicodeString & Str)
+void __fastcall TTerminal::LogEvent(const UnicodeString & Str)
